  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "High-Performance Fixed-Layout Memory Architecture\n\n      [New Features & Low-Level Optimizations]\n      - Introduced 'InitStruct<T>()' to empower the zero-allocation creation of unmanaged structs directly on the raw buffer. It instantly unshifts the pointer to position 0, resizes layout logically, and returns an in-place managed pointer (ref T) for ultra-fast mutations (~0.9 - 1.2 ns).\n      - Introduced 'AsStruct<T>()' and 'AsStruct<T>(long offset)' to achieve Zero-Parse workflows. It overlays an unmanaged struct layout over raw bytes instantly, enabling blazingly fast read/write operations (~0.26 - 0.39 ns).\n      - Integrated full '[MethodImpl(MethodImplOptions.AggressiveInlining)]', 'Unsafe.SizeOf<T>', and 'MemoryMarshal.AsRef<T>' to completely eliminate serialization overhead, reflection, and Garbage Collector pressure (100% Zero-Allocation).",
